Camera V4L2 adapter: raw Bayer capture nodes without an ISP (Qualcomm CAMSS on the OnePlus 6).

Active only for nodes listed in /vendor/etc/camera/camss_raw.cfg; without that file nothing changes, so other
products (rk3568, USB cameras) behave as before. Header-only additions, so the targets that compile these
adapter files need no build change.
- v4l2_fileformat.cpp: a node can match its camera by node name (CAMSS reports driver "qcom-camss" on every
  node); S_FMT sets the raw Bayer format of the node (read from the RDI subdev with format=auto).
- v4l2_buffer.cpp: at DQBUF, convert instead of copying: camss_soft_isp.h (2x2-binning demosaic, black
  level, grey-world white balance, gamma, scaling, I420 BT.601); auto exposure through V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE and
  V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN on the sensor subdev.
- v4l2_dev.cpp: look for the node once more if it appeared after the adapter's init (late sensor probe).
- usb_camera node_utils.cpp: I420 (CAMERA_FORMAT_YCRCB_420_P, what the V4L2 source node delivers) maps to
  AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P for the software scale/codec nodes.

