+/*
+ * Raw Bayer capture nodes (Qualcomm CAMSS RDI and the like) for the V4L2 adapter.
+ *
+ * Active only for cameras listed in /vendor/etc/camera/camss_raw.cfg; without that file
+ * every function below is a no-op and the adapter behaves as before. One line per camera:
+ *
+ *   hw=imx376 video=msm_vfe0_video0 rdi=msm_vfe0_rdi0 sensor=imx376 format=auto black=64
+ *
+ *   hw      hardware name of the sensor in the board's project_hardware.h (DM_C_SENSOR entry)
+ *   video   name of the capture node (/sys/class/video4linux/videoN/name) or a /dev/videoN path
+ *   sensor  optional: name prefix of the sensor subdev (/sys/class/video4linux/v4l-subdevN/name);
+ *           when it can be opened, AE drives V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE / V4L2_CID_ANALOGUE_GAIN on it
+ *   rdi     optional: name of the subdev that feeds the capture node (CAMSS "msm_vfe0_rdi0"); with
+ *           format=auto the raw format and size are read from its pad 0 (VIDIOC_SUBDEV_G_FMT) at
+ *           every stream start, so the Bayer order follows the sensor's flips (IMX376 defaults to
+ *           hflip=vflip=1 = SBGGR10). Explicit width/height/format are the fallback when that fails.
+ *   width/height/format  the raw frame the media graph delivers (format: S{RGGB,GRBG,GBRG,BGGR}
+ *           {8,10,10P,12,12P} or auto); it is what VIDIOC_S_FMT is set to, whatever the pipeline asked
+ *   black   black level in sensor code units (default 64 for 10 bit)
+ *   gain    analogue gain model: sony:<c> (gain = c / (c - code), default sony:512) or
+ *           linear:<unity code>
+ *   ae      on|off (default on), awb on|off (default on), gamma (default 2.2)
+ *
+ * The media graph itself (links, subdev formats) must already be configured (camss_setup at boot,
+ * or media-ctl).
+ * Header only on purpose: v4l2_fileformat.cpp, v4l2_buffer.cpp and v4l2_dev.cpp are compiled by
+ * several targets (usb_camera adapter, board unit tests), none of which needs a BUILD change.
+ */
